.TH SHOWFIGFONTS 1 "June 2026" "FIGdriver\-rs 0.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
showfigfonts \- display a sample rendering of each available FIGfont
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B showfigfonts
[options] [word]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B showfigfonts
scans the configured font directory for FIGfont files and renders a
sample line using each font. By default, the sample line is the font's
own name. A custom word can be provided to render the same text across
all fonts for comparison purposes.
.SH OPTIONS
.B showfigfonts
processes options from left to right; when conflicting options are given,
the last one takes effect.
.TP
.B "\-d, \-\-fontdir"
.IR fontdirectory
Set the font search directory. Defaults to
.IR /usr/share/figlet .
.TP
.B "\-v, \-\-version"
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B "\-h, \-\-help"
Print usage information and exit.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B word
A single word to render with each font. If omitted, each font's own
name is rendered.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Show each font rendering its own name:
.RS
.nf
showfigfonts
.RE
.PP
Render the word \fBtest\fR in every available font:
.RS
.nf
showfigfonts test
.RE
.PP
Scan a custom font directory:
.RS
.nf
showfigfonts \-d /usr/share/fonts/figlet
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FIGLET_FONTDIR
If set, use the given directory as the default font search directory, instead
of
.IR /usr/share/figlet .
This can be overridden with
.BR \-d .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/figlet
Default directory searched for fonts.
.SH NOTES
Unlike the reference showfigfonts, which returns exit status 0 when the
font directory cannot be opened, this implementation returns exit status 1
and prints an error message to stderr.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at <https://github.com/cmatsuoka/figdriver-rs/issues>.
.SH AUTHORS
This
